.TH COLLOQUY 1 "2026-10-14" "colloquy 0.3.0" "News Analysis System"
.SH NAME
colloquy \- ASPIC+ argumentation over dated, sourced evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B colloquy
.I command
.I case
.RI [ literal ]
.RB [ \-\-at
.IR DATE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B colloquy
reads a case file of sourced premises and strict and defeasible rules,
builds every argument the case allows, works out which arguments
defeat which (undermining, rebutting, undercutting, with last-link
preferences), and computes the grounded extension.
Each premise may carry the date it became public, so any past date can
be replayed with
.BR \-\-at ,
given as YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status \fIcase\fR
Status of every question the case tracks.
.TP
.B explain \fIcase literal\fR
The arguments for a literal, with sources, and what defeats them.
.TP
.B whatif \fIcase literal\fR
The premises, rules and critical questions whose defeat would change
the literal's status.
.TP
.B timeline \fIcase\fR
Replays the case one evidence date at a time and prints what changed.
.TP
.B robustness \fIcase\fR
For each topic, the conspiracy number: the smallest number of sources
that would have to be set aside for its status to change, and for a
topic not accepted, how many would have to be set aside for it to become
accepted. Then the priority sensitivity: every verdict that changes if
one priority moves by one.
.B \-\-max \fIN\fR
bounds the size of the sets tried (default 4).
.TP
.B aif \fIcase\fR
Writes the argument graph as Argument Interchange Format JSON.
.TP
.B cases
Lists installed cases.
.SH STATUSES
.TP
.B ACCEPTED
an argument for it survives every attack
.TP
.B REFUTED
an argument for a contrary is accepted
.TP
.B DEFEATED
arguments exist but none survives; this does not mean it is false
.TP
.B CONTESTED
undecided under grounded semantics
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/news-analysis-system/cases/
installed case files; a case can be named without its path or .pl
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLLOQUY_CASE_PATH
colon-separated directories searched for cases before the default
.TP
.B COLLOQUY_LIB
alternative engine file, for running from a source checkout
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
colloquy timeline opera-neutrinos
colloquy status yandex-datacentres-bots
colloquy whatif pentagon-fake-image explosion_at_pentagon \-\-at 2023-05-22T10:06
colloquy explain yandex-datacentres-bots russian_political_bot_activity_fell
colloquy robustness opera-neutrinos \-\-at 2011-09-23
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swipl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Dougherty, with Claude.
